WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.129 --> 00:00:05.759
Hey youtubers It’s charlie, since arrow
and the flash just released this, here it

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:08.490
is, picture teasing their big crossover.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:12.330
I wanted to dedicate a video to explaining
how it’s going to work as well as give a

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:16.240
big update on every single comic book show
DC has in development right now.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.630
Including the ones that they just announced
but haven’t made it to air yet.

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:19.630
Like Supergirl.

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:24.519
Hello any new people, If you just found me
I’m doing arrow and flash videos all season,

00:00:24.519 --> 00:00:28.189
be sure to subscribe to join the team.

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:34.790
Also big heads up, they delayed the arrow
season 2 netflix release because of the dvd.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:39.710
The people that make arrow, like stephen amell,
mark guggenheim the show runner.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:41.570
They have absolutely no say in things like
that.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.630
I don’t want to speak for them, but if there
was a way for them to get episodes to you

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:45.080
faster, they would totally do it.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.640
With that in mind if enough of you want it
I will dedicate a bonus video to a big season

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:50.640
2 recap.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:51.710
Only if you think it’s needed.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:57.190
So just let me know about that in the comments.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.310
Now for some sweet crossover music.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:03.640
This picture is from the table readthrough,
meaning they all sit around giant tables reading

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:04.839
their lines in the script.

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:07.640
Just to explain who’s in this picture and
what’s going on.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:11.719
First off, if you look closely, you can see
Stephen Amell is wearing his Arrow costume

00:01:11.719 --> 00:01:12.719
leather pants.

00:01:12.719 --> 00:01:19.799
They just call them the Arrow pants, which
I think is funny.

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:24.659
Then from left to right there’s Glen Winter
the director of the two episodes, it’s a

00:01:24.659 --> 00:01:25.659
two parter.

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:27.490
Danielle Panabaker who plays Caitlin Snow.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:37.500
She may or may not secretly have powers, David
Ramsay, Jesse Martin who’s playing Detective

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:45.229
West, Candice Patton who is Iris West, and
has her arm wrapped around Emily Bett,

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:51.869
Rick Cosnett who plays Eddie Thawn, keep your
eyes peeled on him, Stephen Amell in his tight

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:57.029
pants, Grant Gustin, Patrick Sabongui who’s
playing the Captain of the Central City police

00:01:57.029 --> 00:01:58.819
department where Barry works,

00:01:58.819 --> 00:02:03.240
Marc Guggenheim who’s the showrunner on
Arrow and Tom Cavanagh, who’s playing Harrison

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.020
Wells, the person who runs Star Labs.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:09.300
The crossover is a little bit different than
what you’re used to.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:16.780
Because both shows are owned by the CW which
is owned by Warner Brothers, which itself

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.340
owns DC Comics and the rights to all DC Universe
characters.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:23.700
The Arrow and Flash people have a few liberties
that other shows don’t.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:27.720
And on top of that, The Flash show was grown
out of Arrow, both in terms of characters

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.100
and in terms of production staff.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:34.660
The people that are writing and running The
Flash originally wrote and produced on Arrow.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:38.110
So they’ll all a big family.

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:40.330
Which is very rare in Television.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:45.780
Structurally the crossover will be a two hour
story broken into two 1 hour parts.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.630
Each of those one hour parts will take place
on each show.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.810
They haven’t formally announced which show
the first part will happen on, but The Flash

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.020
airs first during the week.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:56.971
So if they want to complete the crossover
in a single week, they’ll do part 1 on The

00:02:56.971 --> 00:02:59.920
Flash and part two on Arrow the next day.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.400
That’s what I’m hoping happens, just because
who likes waiting a week to see part 2 of

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.400
anything?

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:11.180
We don’t know what the story device will
be that will merit Team Arrow being on The

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.350
Flash show and Team Flash being on the Arrow
Show.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:17.380
It’s possible they could pick an event out
of the comics to use or it could be some original

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:18.380
event.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:24.250
The Flash as a show is sticking very close
to the Flash Rebirth storyline, but Arrow

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:27.100
plays a little more fast and loose with the
comics.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:31.220
What you can plan on is one or two characters
from each show going on the other show.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:34.430
They won’t have every single member of team
arrow and team flash on screen at the same

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:35.430
time.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.190
Logistically it would be a nightmare.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:42.160
Since last year’s mid-season finale turned
Barry Allen into the Flash, I would bet on

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.760
something major happening.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:47.080
Like the reveal of the Reverse Flash or Zoom,
or however they’ll defining the big bad

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.080
on that show.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.440
I’ll talk more about that character in a
separate Flash video.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:55.130
But of all the big reveals they could make
there’s The Reverse Flash, Brandon Routh’s

00:03:55.130 --> 00:04:00.230
Ray Palmer could join Team Arrow full on,
he could also get his supersuit, the Rogues

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:04.660
could come together as a team for the first
time and we could see Ra’s Al Ghul for the

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:05.660
first time.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:13.720
Any one of those things could happen or a
couple of them at the same time.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:18.750
They didn’t cast Ra’s Al Ghul till after
they shot the first episode, so he’s not

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:31.380
going to be in the premiere.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.960
Which reminds me, they just cast Captain Boomerang
on Arrow.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:46.600
He’ll probably get tied up in a Suicide
Squad storyline.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:52.680
But the actor the cast, Nick Tarabay, was
also on Spartacus with Manu Bennett.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.360
I like the meta thing going on.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.980
Captain Boomerang has both been a member of
The Rogues in the Flash comics and The Suicide

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:58.980
Squad.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.380
So it’s possible his character could be
involved in the crossover episode.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:09.000
Some other big happenings: Brandon Routh,
like I said could possibly get his Atom Suit

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.090
during the midseason finale.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:17.280
He just did an interview where he explained
they’d just finished shooting 6 episodes

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:22.080
and he’d seen concept art of it.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:28.480
I’d plan on it looking closer to something
like this but without the super bright colors.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:29.600
Just toned down a little.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:34.070
The midseason finale will be episode 9 of
each show, so his interview was from a couple

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:35.070
weeks ago.

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:37.740
It does take them a while to make those special
suits like Roy’s and Oliver’s, so we might

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.010
not see The Atom’s till right before the
last episode next year.

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:44.640
In terms of character arcs, Brandon Routh
said most of his scenes in those first six

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.590
episodes are just with Felicity.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:50.740
Meaning, we’ll see a lot of Felicity and
Ray Palmer doing things without Oliver around.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:56.560
I feel like people will love Ray Palmer, but
hate Ray Palmer and Felicity.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.360
Maybe not everyone, but he’s going to be
a romantic foil for oliver.

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:02.810
Brandon Routh said it’s his job to come
between Felicity and Oliver, so he’s looking

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:03.810
forward to the fan response whether you love
the new ‘ship or totally hate on it.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:06.169
Oliver is the real protagonist of the series,
so ultimately we root for him.

00:06:06.169 --> 00:06:11.200
So when someone comes between him and Felicity,
of course we’re supposed to not like it.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:15.810
Speaking of Felicity though, Mark Guggenheim
has been teasing some Felicity Related Behind

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:16.840
the scenes stuff.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:18.220
First he posted this picture.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.210
It’s the inside of Felicity’s Apartment.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:23.120
Tumblr went nuts with this.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:25.310
Just look at the poster above her TV.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:27.430
Robin Hood, totally appropriate.

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:30.550
Then just as I was making this video, like
literally in the last hour.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:31.960
He also posted this image.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:34.760
It’s a sign from Sherwood Florist.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:38.770
In the Longbow Hunters story in the comics,
when Oliver Queen and Black Canary moved from

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:43.680
Star City to Seattle, Black Canary got a flower
shop and named it Sherwood Florist.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.870
The two of them lived in an apartment above
the shop.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:50.820
The building the shop was in served as their
base of operations, so Arrow could turn Sherwood

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:58.449
Florist into the new Verdant for the arrow
cave or it could just be where felicity’s

00:06:58.449 --> 00:06:59.490
apartment is located.

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:03.580
In the trailer we saw her working a nerd herd
looking job, so I don’t think she owns the

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:05.410
flower shop like in the comics.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:08.000
Just as a big reminder.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:15.169
Arrow and Flash Premiere in 3 weeks.

00:07:15.169 --> 00:07:20.690
The Flash is on Tuesday nights and Arrow on
Wednesday’s.

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:21.730
Both at 8PM Eastern Time.

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:29.160
I know a lot of you in international countries
aren’t sure when you’ll get new episodes.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:35.670
But just check the channel listings for wherever
they normally broadcast Arrow episodes.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:40.790
Now, here’s the details for all the new
Comic Book Shows DC has in development, these

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:42.800
are the ones that aren’t on air yet:

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:47.259
First up there’s a new super dark animated
version of Justice League from Bruce Timm.

00:07:47.259 --> 00:07:51.380
If you’re not familiar with him, he’s
basically the guy behind all the best DC Comics

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:56.830
animated shows like Batman the Animated Series,
Batman Mask of the Phantasm, Batman Beyond

00:07:56.830 --> 00:08:00.020
and the Justice League cartoon from about
10 years ago.

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:03.770
When they say darker version, think of it
being more like Batman the Animated Series

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:05.110
in terms of tone.

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:07.050
No word on when we’ll get to see this.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:13.009
It takes up to 6 months to animate a single
episode, so it might be 2016 before we see

00:08:13.009 --> 00:08:14.009
anything.

00:08:14.009 --> 00:08:16.820
Then there’s the live action Teen Titans,
they’re just calling it Titans.

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:21.000
I already did a video about this so I’ll
add a link in the description.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.652
That’s still in the pilot stage.

00:08:23.652 --> 00:08:25.630
Next there’s Supergirl from Greg Berlanti
and a co-writer.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:30.340
Berlanti is also the guy behind Arrow and
the Flash and a whole bunch of other new non-comic

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:32.709
book shows.

00:08:32.709 --> 00:08:36.450
They are still getting ready to shop it to
networks.

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:40.649
It won’t be on the CW and the show won’t
be called Supergirl.

00:08:40.649 --> 00:08:48.040
If things do work out I would plan on seeing
this in fall 2016 maybe 2017.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:52.450
Next is Hourman, Geoff Johns announced last
year the CW was developing an Hourman show

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:53.450
based on the dc comics character.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:57.620
It’s been 10 months with no news, so this
project could be dead.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:00.380
And if the CW isn’t going to do wonder woman.

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:02.870
It’s possible the Hourman project could
move to a different network.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:06.230
Fox Networks, the same people making Gotham
just bought the rights to Lucifer.

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.550
They’ll be turning that into a live action
show.

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:11.930
The character Lucifer Morningstar originated
in Neil Gaiman’s Sandman comics and eventually

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:13.760
got his own spin off comic.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:17.740
Fox just bought the rights, so we probably
won’t see this till 2017.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:20.890
Next is Preacher, it’s based on the comic
by Garth Ennis.

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:22.380
Seth Rogen and Adam Goldberg.

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:24.820
These two guys are developing this for AMC.

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:28.020
A showrunner and executive producers have
been hired.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:30.530
So this seems like it’s moving along nicely.

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:33.620
But I wouldn’t plan on seeing any news about
it till next year.

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:36.350
With maybe a 2016 premiere date.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:41.640
Scapled, the Vertigo comic is in development
at the WGN network, it’s being described

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:44.200
as the Sopranos on a native american reservation.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:49.240
There isn’t a showrunner yet, so they’re
probably still working on pilot scripts.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:53.110
DMZ, another vertigo comic, is in development
at SyFY.

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:58.410
It takes place in a post-civil war New York
City, Which has been turned into a Demilitarized

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.530
Zone, thus the DMZ title.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:06.750
Syfy is also turning Frank Miller’s Ronin
comic into a miniseries.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:11.920
It’s about a Ronin Samurai who failed to
protect his master from a demon.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:15.610
He wakes up 800 years later in modern day
in the body of a new person and has to fight

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:18.090
the same demon for control of a magical sword.

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:19.950
As of right now that’s it.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:27.361
Usually this is the time of the year when
networks buy new shows, so if any new comic

00:10:27.361 --> 00:10:30.880
book shows get announced it probably won’t
be till next year.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:32.230
Here’s the big question though.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:34.120
Of all the new shows I just listed.

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:35.740
Which are you most excited to see?

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:40.160
Right now I’m really looking forward to
that new Animated Justice League.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:44.139
My next video will be for constantine, I’ll
be doing a breakdown of the character and

00:10:44.139 --> 00:10:48.060
the series for people who have never read
the comic.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:49.410
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:52.540
I have seen the first episode, so I’ll post
a review next week.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.940
It’s not premiering till the end of october
so it’s still a long ways off.

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:56.720
Right now click here to get that explainer
video.

